{"name":"Hinterland","hex":"#616c51","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hinterland","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The land immediately next to, and inland from, a coast.","The rural territory surrounding an urban area, especially a port."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hinterland"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hinterland","blocks":[{"text":"Hinterland is the area under the influence of a particular human settlement. The word comes from a German word meaning 'land behind' a city, a port, or similar. Its use in English was first documented by the geographer George Chisholm in his Handbook of Commercial Geography (1888). Originally the term was associated with the area of a port in which materials for export and import are stored and shipped. Subsequently, the use of the word expanded to its current use."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hinterland","wikidata":"Q4354"},{"title":"Hinterland (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Hinterland, known as Y Gwyll in the original Welsh language version, is a Welsh language noir police procedural series broadcast on S4C in Welsh from 29 October 2013. The main character, DCI Tom Mathias, is played by Richard Harrington. On 27 November 2013, a second series was announced by S4C. The English-language version, with brief passages of Welsh dialogue, aired on BBC One Wales. When it was shown on the BBC in 2014, it was the first BBC television drama with dialogue in both English and Welsh. A third series of the show began filming in January 2016 and debuted on S4C on 30 October."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/54/Hinterland_-_season_1_DVD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hinterland_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q15129848"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"hinterland":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d3/En-au-hinterland.ogg?utm_sou